  {
    "number": 249,
    "title": "Refresh the work guide to current GitHub status",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nBring the cross-project work guide fully up to date before public publication. This builds on [Hub PR #248](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/248), which merged a parallel refresh while this PR was in review. Round 1 (`73f5e61`) refreshed from the older base `28f7599` and conflicted with #248. This candidate is rebased onto #248's merge `f89d42a` and reconciled. It keeps #248's guide assignments and prose, and adds only what #248 did not cover.\n\n- **Snapshot.** Backlog read at 2026-09-24 23:35 UTC: 118 open issues (Hub 66, Nanoleaf 33, Pixoo 19). The open set and every primary assignment are unchanged from #248. Merged-work history read at 23:35 UTC from Hub `f89d42a`, Nanoleaf `9e2c413` and Pixoo `0ca009c`; it now includes #248.\n- **Archive.** Adds completed-milestone rows for work closed since the last edition: Hub #231 (one-step settings) and #237 (scope defaults), and Nanoleaf #108 (thread links), #78 (default layout), #133 (availability decision) and the Lively closure (#134). Replaces \"Archive removal continues in #218\" with the issue's current scope.\n- **Engineering maintenance tracks.** That guide's 16 issues now split into Hub, Nanoleaf and Pixoo tracks, as Adding devices already does. The generator now fails if a track list leaves out a guide row; before, such a row silently disappeared. A new maintenance test covers that failure.\n- **Roadmap.** Removes several same-track arrows that implied order between independent issues:\n  - Hub #241 and Nanoleaf #111 no longer follow Nanoleaf #90.\n  - The renderer decision no longer follows the deferred ambient view.\n  - Hub gates no longer follow the Nanoleaf architecture node.\n  - Nanoleaf #131 and #132 share one node.\n\n  The Nanoleaf architecture order now starts with #118, and the investigations sit in a later column. Nanoleaf #121 has its own node, with cross edges for its recorded start condition (#118, then #111, #112 and #115). Session retirement reads #218, then #241, then Nanoleaf #110. The tracks that `reconcile()` appended now live in `TRACKS`.\n- **Prose.** Hub #218 now says the archive trial passed, but a non-archive end did not retire its session and the cause is under investigation. Nanoleaf #135's design is recorded as settled, not pending. Nanoleaf #100 lists its three open decisions under Blockers and decisions. Topic next steps now name Hub #244, #247 and #242, Nanoleaf #113 and #132, and Pixoo #79. The Hub #218 next step is dropped: that issue is in review and blocked, so it could never appear. The reading notes for the new issues are more specific.\n- **Checks.** The live-status and badge fixtures use Nanoleaf #47 (open and deferred, long-lived) instead of the newly filed #92. The blocker-injection test uses Hub #222 and first checks that it is a next step.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py` passed at head `5a07b92bc226b0124df724e4f3e3ad382213cb51`. Rebuilding after commit produced no output drift. Guide SHA-256: `2d56cce189fbe45087d07ad344b9d1af88af67349d48dcf0968319717393e5d7`.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py` passed (13 tests).\n- `node docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs` passed (Node 24.21.0, Playwright 1.63.0, Chromium 1243). The two console errors it logs are its own simulated 429 and aborted requests.\n- I inspected the roadmap, the Engineering maintenance, Nanoleaf wall map, monitoring and hosting guides, and the opening lists at 1440 and 390 px.\n- `git diff --check` passed. All 18 changed paths are under `docs/work-guide/`. Diagrams and the atlas are unchanged.\n- Screenshots, the print PDF and the verification logs are kept outside Git in the main checkout at `.local/evidence/guide-publish-20260924b/`.\n\n## Reviews\n\nRound 1 at `73f5e61`: independent Standards and Specification reviews.\n- **Standards:** found the stale base and conflict with #248 (P1), fixed by this rebase. Its P3s are also fixed: the cross edges into the combined #120/#121 node, the short-lived fixture, and the untested exact-cover assertion.\n- **Specification:** found three P2s, all fixed here: #135 shown as awaiting a decision, the Nanoleaf architecture order, and the #131 → #132 arrow. Its P3s are fixed too: the #218 wording, the #100 decisions, the grouped-node arrows and the Sony wording.\n- **One P3 kept on purpose:** control fixes such as Hub #247 still sit after the UI foundation on the main product path. That column order predates this PR, and changing the main path is outside this refresh.\n\nRound 2 reviews of `f89d42a..5a07b92` are pending.\n\n## UI approval and guide-only CI\n\n- **Affected UI:** the generated guide only. All paths are under `docs/work-guide/`, so the [guide UI exemption](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/blob/main/docs/sdlc.md#ui-approval-scope) applies.\n- **Guide-only CI exception:** the receipt follows as a PR comment.\n\n## Known gaps (owner follow-ups)\n\n- Nanoleaf #120 and #121, and still #16, #19 and #20, carry `blocked` labels whose prerequisites appear only in their bodies, so the guide shows \"Reconcile the issue body\" for them. Hub #218's `blocked` label is intentional while its live acceptance is investigated, but the generic gate text shows the same message. This PR adds no native blocked-by links; that tracker write needs the owner's go-ahead.\n- A2 (system map) and the BUNNY atlas still carry evidence notes from their earlier pin, as earlier editions recorded.\n\nThis is a dated snapshot. It installs nothing and operates no devices. The public publication PR follows after reviews, merge and the guide-only CI receipt.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
